<title>GERMANY: Germany's Stoiber-better EMU delay than weak Euro.</title>
<headline>Germany's Stoiber-better EMU delay than weak Euro.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bavarian premier Edmund Stoiber said after a meeting with Italian Prime Minister Romano Prodi on Monday that he favoured a delay in the single European currency project rather than the risk of a weak Euro.</p>
<p>&quot;A weak Euro wouldn't help anyone,&quot; Stoiber said at a news briefing afterwards.</p>
<p>Prodi had earlier said on Monday that Italy would not require the criteria be weakened to join monetary union nor a delay in the planned January 1999 start for the euro currency.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
